      },
      "worked": "Join the centre to every vertex. The regular polygon is divided into $n$ congruent isosceles triangles, each with two sides of length $r$ and central angle $\\theta$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=\\frac{360^\\circ}{n}.\\end{align*}$$\nBy the triangle area rule, the area $T$ of each triangle is\n$$\\begin{align*}T&=\\frac12r^2\\sin\\left(\\frac{360^\\circ}{n}\\right).\\end{align*}$$\nSumming the $n$ triangle areas,\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=n\\left[\\frac12r^2\\sin\\left(\\frac{360^\\circ}{n}\\right)\\right]\\\\A&=\\frac{nr^2}{2}\\sin\\left(\\frac{360^\\circ}{n}\\right).\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
